// Reactivity S1 — a `signal(v)` is a mutable reactive cell. `.get()` reads it, `.set(v)` updates it.
// With no `computed`/`effect` yet, a signal is still observable through get-after-set: the read
// reflects the last write. The value type rides in `Signal<T>`, so `.get()` recovers it (here `int`
// then `string`). A self-update `s.set(s.get() + 1)` reads and writes the same cell in one line.
// expect: stdout "0"
// expect: stdout "42"
// expect: stdout "hi"
// expect: stdout "43"
// expect: exit 0
s = signal(0)
echo s.get()
s.set(42)
echo s.get()
name = signal("hi")
echo name.get()
s.set(s.get() + 1)
echo s.get()
